# Security (Node.js API)

## Helmet

- Use Helmet middleware for secure headers (X-Content-Type-Options, X-Frame-Options, etc.); configure CSP if needed

## CORS

- Restrict origin to known frontends; allow only needed methods and headers; credentials only when required
- Do not use `*` with credentials

## Rate Limiting

- Apply rate limit (e.g. express-rate-limit) per IP or per user; different limits for auth vs API; return 429 with Retry-After when appropriate

## CSRF

- For cookie-based sessions, use CSRF tokens on state-changing requests; SameSite cookie attribute; validate token on POST/PUT/DELETE

## Input & Output

- Validate and sanitize input at boundaries; use parameterized queries (ORM); escape output for HTML if rendering; see input-sanitization.mdc
- Never log secrets or full tokens

## Secrets

- Env vars or secret manager; never in code; rotate regularly; use different secrets per environment

## Conventions

- HTTPS only in prod; secure headers; least privilege; validate and sanitize input; no secrets in logs

## Anti-Patterns

- Permissive CORS; no rate limiting; trusting client input; secrets in repo

**See also:** `input-sanitization.mdc`, `auth.mdc`, `../../patterns/security.mdc`
